<LegalPage title="Accessibility" updated="October 3, 2026" intro="We want everyone to be able to read, listen to and use ThereYouAreJesus.com.">
  <p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA, and we keep accessibility in mind as the site grows.</p>
  <h2>What we've done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The whole site works with a keyboard, with a visible focus outline and a "Skip to content" link.</li>
    <li>Menus, the Seven Spirits, the audio player and forms are labeled for screen readers.</li>
    <li>Text is high contrast on a dark background, and pages adapt to phones, tablets and zoomed-in screens.</li>
    <li>If you've asked your device to reduce motion, the stars, flames and other animations stay still.</li>
    <li>The audio player supports your device's media controls and lock screen.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>Some older posts may have images without descriptions, and third-party radio streams and podcasts are provided by others. We're working through older content over time.</p>
  <h2>Tell us what isn't working</h2>
  <p>If something is hard to use, email <a href="mailto:john@thereyouarejesus.com">john@thereyouarejesus.com</a> with the page and what happened. We'll reply within a few business days and help you get the content another way in the meantime.</p>
</LegalPage>
